---
import DocsLayout from "../../components/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Wishlists — mgz-pkmn docs"
  description="Wishlists in mgz-pkmn: one-tap Want to save a card you're chasing, organize into named lists, set an optional price cap, and settle the chase when you own it."
  current="/docs/wishlists"
  icon="footprints"
  accent="sun"
  eyebrow="Your stuff"
  heading="Wishlists"
  lede={'A wishlist is a list of cards you\'re hunting — "I want these." It\'s the chasing half of your library, and it\'s where a show prep list usually starts.'}
>
  <h2 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">
    Want a card, one tap
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-coconut-500 dark:text-sand-300">
    Every card — in Search results, Browse, Swipe, and the detail view — carries a
    one-tap <strong class="font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">Want</strong>
    action. Tapping it drops the card onto your default wishlist, <em>My wishlist</em>,
    created the first time you use it. Tap again to remove. Capture first, organize
    later — no picker in the way.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">
    Organize into named lists
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-coconut-500 dark:text-sand-300">
    When the default bucket isn't where you want it, open a card's detail view and
    use <strong class="font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">Add to a list…</strong>
    to file it onto a specific wishlist, with an inline create option. In
    <a href="/docs/browse" class="text-palm-500 hover:text-palm-400 dark:text-sun-300 dark:hover:text-sun-200 underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Browse</a>,
    a set header's <strong class="font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">New ▾</strong>
    can spin up a wishlist seeded from the whole set. Wishlists live in the
    <a href="/docs/binders" class="text-palm-500 hover:text-palm-400 dark:text-sun-300 dark:hover:text-sun-200 underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Binders</a>
    tab of your <a href="/docs/backpack" class="text-palm-500 hover:text-palm-400 dark:text-sun-300 dark:hover:text-sun-200 underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Backpack</a>,
    each row tagged with a <strong class="font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">Chasing</strong> badge.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">
    A price you'd pay
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-coconut-500 dark:text-sand-300">
    Wishlist items can carry an optional price cap — the number you'd want to be
    alerted at. It's saved with the card today; price alerting itself is a separate
    feature still to come.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50">
    Settling the chase
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-coconut-500 dark:text-sand-300">
    Open a wishlist to drill into its cards. When you finally land one you were
    chasing, marking it owned settles the chase rather than yanking the row out
    from under you. Delete a whole wishlist from its Backpack row's two-step trash
    control.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-palm-300 bg-palm-50 p-5 dark:border-sun-300/40 dark:bg-sun-300/5">
    <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-coconut-600 dark:text-sand-200">
      The flip side is <a href="/docs/collections" class="text-palm-500 hover:text-palm-400 dark:text-sun-300 dark:hover:text-sun-200 underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Collections</a> —
      the same shape, opposite meaning: "I own these."
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
